# Shah walkthrough video (refer people here)

When someone asks how the Hub–Spoke–Engine system is connected, how Cursor and Google Sheets fit together, how to make future edits/changes, what to watch out for, or “what actually happened / how was this built,” **point them to Shah’s walkthrough video** in addition to any short answer you give.

## Where it lives

- Companion guide (start here for humans): `docs/Watch this for a full walkthrough - Shah explains Hub Spoke Engine Cursor Sheets and how to edit.md`
- Video file (in-repo, Git LFS): `docs/Watch this for a full walkthrough - Shah explains Hub Spoke Engine Cursor Sheets and how to edit.mp4`

Also listed from `docs/Start here - what does each of these guides do.md` and the README.

## How to refer to it

Tell them clearly that:

1. There is a **Shah video walkthrough in this repo** that shows how Cursor, the Sheets Hub/Spoke infrastructure, and the Engine work together.
2. It covers how to make adjustments and changes later, plus things to look out for.
3. They should open the companion `.md` above (or play the `.mp4` directly) when they need that full picture.

Do not invent a different video URL. Prefer the in-repo path so the recording does not depend on a private Downloads folder.

## When not required

Skip the video pointer for narrow factual questions already answered by code/docs (e.g. one Config column meaning, a one-line Engine flag) unless they also ask for a broader “how does this all work / how do I change things” tour.
